1" 13194139534883 true] [17592186317221 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534883 true] [17592186317221 1100 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(1,1,-1)$, $P(3,4,2)$ and $Q(-1,2,0).$\n\n$\\,y\\,-\\,z\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$=0$" 13194139534883 true] [17592186317221 1113 #uuid "3f2ff546-7761-5f3a-872c-3eb0b39a7e47" 13194139534883 true] [17592186317221 1145 "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,P$ and $Q$ are $a=⟨1,1,-1⟩,\\,p=⟨3,4,2⟩,$ and $q=⟨-1,2,0⟩.$\n\nFirst, using the $3$ points we build $2$ vectors parallel to the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} & =\\overset{\\to }{AP} \\\\  & =⟨3,4,2⟩-⟨1,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,3,3⟩ \\\\ {v}_{2} & =\\overset{\\to }{AQ} \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,0⟩-⟨1,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow,  we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =0i-8j+8k \\\\  & =⟨0,-8,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,-8,8⟩ & =⟨3,4,2⟩\\cdot ⟨0,-8,8⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,-8,8⟩ & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨0,-8,8⟩ & =-16 \\\\ -8y+8z & =-16 \\\\ -8y+8z+16 & =0 \\\\ y-z-2 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534883 true] [17592186317222 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317223 13194139534883 true] [17592186317222 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534883 true] [17592186317222 1041 "field-1" 13194139534883 true] [17592186317222 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317223 13194139534883 true] [17592186317222 1110 